                        current.right = Node(value)
                        break
                    current = current.right
```

In the `add_value` method, the provided code snippet is extended to handle the case when the value to be added is greater than or equal to the current node's value. If the value is greater, the traversal continues to the right child, and if the right child is None, a new node is added as the right child. This ensures that the binary search tree property is maintained.

